# Keep LF line endings in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true, which is the default from
# Git for Windows' installer) rewrites text files as CRLF during checkout.
# Only files that actually differ between the branches get rewritten, so a
# branch switch leaves the tree in a *mixed* state — some files LF, some CRLF.
# Prettier defaults to endOfLine: "lf" and then reports every line of every
# converted file as an error, which looks like the whole codebase broke at
# once. This happened on 2026-08-10 during the dev -> main merge: 10 files
# were converted and lint went from 0 errors to 3290.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf for this repository, so contributors on
# Windows, macOS, and Linux all get the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never apply line-ending conversion.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.phar  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
